// Nothing but data: one table per language, keyed by the English source string
// (see Strings, which is the lookup around this). English itself has no table -
// it is what a missing key falls back to, so adding a string to the shell
// costs nothing here until somebody translates it.
//
// Every table carries the same keys in the same order, grouped by where the
// string shows up, so a missing one is visible as a gap rather than having to
// be diffed for. Two rules the tables have to keep, both about layout rather
// than about language:
//
//  - a "hint" (the muted line under a settings row) has to fit on one line
//    within the 780px column, so those are written to fit rather than
//    translated literally - roughly 140 Latin characters at the 11px they
//    render at. Nothing enforces this; the row elides past its width instead
//    of wrapping, and an elided hint is a translation that needs shortening.
//  - a "value" (what sits between a row's ‹ › arrows) shares its width with
//    the Navigation tab's chord boxes, which grow to fit the longest one (see
//    ui/Metrics.qml). A long value doesn't overflow, but it does widen every
//    keybind box on that tab, so these stay terse.
